flowchart TD
    box_0(["Start"])
    box_1["Collect five parts with detected burrs. Inspect the<br/>burr location and orientation using a magnifier to<br/>determine whether it is at the insertion lead<br/>chamfer or on the cylindrical press fit surface."]
    box_2{"Is the burr present on parts before they enter the<br/>assembly process (incoming material defect)?"}
    box_3["Inspect parts from the supply conveyor input side<br/>before they reach the assembly station to confirm<br/>the burr is present in the incoming material."]
    box_4["Quarantine the current input batch. Create a non<br/>conformance record for the incoming material and<br/>notify the quality assurance team. Reload from a<br/>confirmed conforming batch."]
    box_5{"Is the burr present on all processed parts or only<br/>on parts from a specific pressing cycle?"}
    box_6["Run a slow test cycle and inspect parts at the press<br/>output for every five cycles to determine whether<br/>the burr pattern is consistent or linked to a<br/>specific machine phase."]
    box_7["If the burr correlates with a specific cycle phase,<br/>identify the tooling component responsible (pressing<br/>head edge, guide surface, or nest edge) and inspect<br/>it immediately."]
    box_8{"Does the pressing head edge have an acceptable<br/>chamfer condition (no sharp edge or chipping)?"}
    box_9["Inspect the pressing head leading edge under<br/>magnification for chipping, sharp transitions, or<br/>material build up that could be transferred to the<br/>part."]
    box_10["Replace the pressing head or have the edge<br/>repolished to the specified chamfer radius. Verify<br/>the edge condition before resuming."]
    box_11{"Is the press guide alignment free of lateral offset<br/>(no side loading of the pressing head against the<br/>part)?"}
    box_12["Check the lateral clearance of the pressing head in<br/>the guide bushing. Verify that the pressing head<br/>moves without radial contact against the guide wall<br/>during descent."]
    box_13["Realign the press guide bushing to eliminate lateral<br/>offset. Verify alignment with a test pressing cycle<br/>before resuming production."]
    box_14["Quarantine all affected parts and record the root<br/>cause and corrective action in the quality log.<br/>Notify quality assurance team with sample parts for<br/>disposition."]
    box_15{"Is the root cause of the burr an incoming material<br/>defect requiring a supplier corrective action?"}
    box_16["Complete the following steps: 1. Compile defect data<br/>for the affected batch: quantity, rejection rate,<br/>and spec limit. 2. Cross-reference rejections<br/>against the production schedule to identify the<br/>batch window. 3. Confirm whether any burred parts<br/>were released to downstream assembly."]
    box_17[/"Refer to the supplier corrective action request<br/>procedure."/]
    box_18{"Were any burred parts released to downstream<br/>assembly or shipped before detection?"}
    box_19["Trace all parts from the burr fault window through<br/>downstream stations and customer delivery records.<br/>Quarantine any located parts."]
    box_20["Issue customer advisory notice if any burred parts<br/>reached shipment, notify quality assurance manager."]
    box_21(["End, Customer advisory issued. quality assurance<br/>disposition and supplier CA monitoring required."])
    box_22(["End, Notify quality assurance team and maintenance<br/>team. Procedure complete."])

